{"id":"h21t3","name":"Team Size at Every Level","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>employees</b> has the columns <code>emp_id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>manager_id</code> (<code>NULL</code> for the top of the company) and <code>salary</code>. There is no cycle. A <code>manager_id</code> that does not exist in the table is treated like <code>NULL</code>.</p>\n<p>The <b>team</b> of an employee is everybody below them, at any level: their direct reports, the reports of their reports, and so on (the employee is not in their own team).</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for every employee with at least one direct report, the columns <code>emp_id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>level</code> (1 for an employee with no manager, 2 for their direct reports, and so on), <code>team_size</code>, <code>team_salary</code> (total salary of the team) and <code>depth</code> (the number of levels below them: 1 when nobody in their team has reports), sorted by <code>team_salary</code> from the highest, then <code>emp_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>employees</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>emp_id</th><th>name</th><th>manager_id</th><th>salary</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Nadia</td><td>null</td><td>9000</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Yao</td><td>1</td><td>6000</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Lina</td><td>1</td><td>6500</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Omar</td><td>2</td><td>4000</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Awa</td><td>2</td><td>4200</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Kofi</td><td>4</td><td>3000</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Sami</td><td>3</td><td>3900</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Ines</td><td>99</td><td>5000</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Theo</td><td>8</td><td>3100</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>emp_id</th><th>name</th><th>level</th><th>team_size</th><th>team_salary</th><th>depth</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Nadia</td><td>1</td><td>6</td><td>27600</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Yao</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>11200</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Lina</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>3900</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Ines</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3100</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Omar</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>3000</td><td>1</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>employees</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>emp_id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>level</code>, <code>team_size</code>, <code>team_salary</code>, <code>depth</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["CTE récursive","hiérarchie","profondeur","managers sans chef","agrégats sur toute la descendance"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>employees</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>emp_id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>level</code>, <code>team_size</code>, <code>team_salary</code>, <code>depth</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"employees":{"columns":[["emp_id","INT"],["name","TEXT"],["manager_id","INT"],["salary","INT"]],"rows":[[1,"Nadia",null,9000],[2,"Yao",1,6000],[3,"Lina",1,6500],[4,"Omar",2,4000],[5,"Awa",2,4200],[6,"Kofi",4,3000],[7,"Sami",3,3900],[8,"Ines",99,5000],[9,"Theo",8,3100]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["emp_id","name","level","team_size","team_salary","depth"],"rows":[[1,"Nadia",1,6,27600,3],[2,"Yao",2,3,11200,2],[3,"Lina",2,1,3900,1],[8,"Ines",1,1,3100,1],[4,"Omar",3,1,3000,1]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"employees":{"columns":[["emp_id","INT"],["name","TEXT"],["manager_id","INT"],["salary","INT"]],"rows":[[10,"A",null,1],[11,"B",10,1],[12,"C",11,1],[13,"D",12,1],[20,"E",null,5],[21,"F",20,3]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["emp_id","name","level","team_size","team_salary","depth"],"rows":[[10,"A",1,3,3,3],[20,"E",1,1,3,1],[11,"B",2,2,2,2],[12,"C",3,1,1,1]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}